# UST.G3CT: Selected Connection-Action First-Jet Theorem

## Statement

Let `b` be the fixed selected G3CC B103 H02 source and let `K(a)` denote the
complete recursively reduced connection action in the moving quotient charts.
At the selected proof fiber, UST.G3CT computes

```text
K'(0) b.
```

The computation uses the complete UST.G3CS pole-six return derivative, the
selected UST.G3BQ base preimages and the exact UST.G3BK family-update matrices.
It solves, in order,

```text
M_H02 c'_H02 = R'_H02 - M'_H02 c_H02,image,
M_H11 c'_H11 = D_1/4(c'_H02,image) - M'_H11 c_H11,image,
M_H20 c'_H20 = D_1/3(c'_H11,image) - M'_H20 c_H20,image.
```

Every reconstructed equation has zero residual.  The quotient derivatives
contain 228 H02, 931 H11 and 222 H20 nonzero entries.  In canonical B103 order
they give one exact `1509 x 1` vector with 1,381 nonzero entries.  The terminal
H20 image divergence is identically zero.

## Meaning

This is the first complete derivative of the actual selected connection action
on one physical source, rather than a static endpoint operator, a frozen-frame
proxy, or the quotient correction alone.  The latter differs from the full
answer in 1,379 coordinates.

The theorem intentionally computes only `K'(0)b`; a full `1509 x 1509`
derivative is unnecessary for one-source integration.  Characteristic-zero or
interval promotion along G3BJ, the initial integral-class embedding and the
terminal period/`beta_C` readout remain separate obligations.

